WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.103
Host: Distinguish chemical transmission from
temporal and spatial summation.

2
00:00:05.103 --> 00:00:11.682
Guide: Chemical transmission releases a
transmitter that changes postsynaptic
signalling or conductance.

3
00:00:11.682 --> 00:00:19.585
Guide: Temporal summation combines closely
timed inputs; spatial summation combines
inputs at different sites.

4
00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:24.563
Guide: Their combined effect helps determine
whether the receiving neuron fires.

5
00:00:24.563 --> 00:00:30.817
Host: Repeated small inputs at the same
synapse arrive close together and have a
larger combined

6
00:00:30.817 --> 00:00:34.096
Host: effect. What is this?

7
00:00:34.096 --> 00:00:41.014
Guide: Temporal summation. Temporal summation
combines effects of closely timed inputs.
